1) Display EMPNO, ENAME, SAL, DNAME and LOC using NATURAL JOIN
SELECT employee_id,
first_name,
salary,
department_name,
location_id
FROM Employees
NATURAL JOIN Departments;

2) Display JOB, MGR, SAL, COMM, DNAME for Employees Whose JOB is SALESMAN
SELECT job_id,
manager_id,
salary,
commission_pct,
department_name
FROM Employees
JOIN Departments
ON Employees.department_id = Departments.department_id
WHERE job_id='SALESMAN';

3) Display ENAME, JOB, DEPTNO and DNAME for Employees Working in DALLAS

Since your table uses location_id instead of LOC, we assume:

1900 = DALLAS

Query:

SELECT first_name,
job_id,
Employees.department_id,
department_name
FROM Employees
JOIN Departments
ON Employees.department_id = Departments.department_id
WHERE location_id = 1900;

4) Display All Employees Including King (No Manager) Ordered by Employee Number
SELECT employee_id,
first_name,
manager_id,
salary
FROM Employees
ORDER BY employee_id;
